029464","urn:scms:0188600505740"],"publish_date":"August 23, 2002","works":[{"key":"/works/OL4272872W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"According to tradition, the great medieval Svetambara Jain scholar-monk Haribhadra was in his early years a learned brahman who boasted that he would become the pupil of anyone whose teachings he could not controvert."},"lccn":["2002074329"],"ocaid":"jains0000dund_2edi","oclc_numbers":["49594164","1259200384"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Jainism is one of the world's oldest religious traditions. Is it still a living and dynamic faith?\".\n\n\"The Indian religion of Jainism, whose central tenet involves nonviolence to all creatures, is one of the world's oldest and at the same time least-understood faiths. Paul Dundas looks at Jainism in its social and doctrinal context, discusses its history, sects, scriptures and ritual, and describes how the Jains have, over two and a half thousand years, defined themselves as a unique religious community.\".\n\n\"This revised and expanded edition takes account of new research into Jainism as carried out over the last ten years.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":18,"revision":18,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-02-05T05:26:53.400500"}}},"ISBN:9780415266055":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780415266055","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7489143M/The_Jains_(Library_of_Religious_Beliefs_and_Practices)","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7489143M/The_Jains_(Library_of_Religious_Beliefs_and_Practices)","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1212935-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Routledge"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["658965"]},"covers":[1212935],"lc_classifications":["BL1351.3.D86 2002"],"key":"/books/OL7489143M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL828111A","name":"Paul Dundas"}],"languages":[{"key":"/langu